                        "content": "     1\u2192# Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.\n     2\u2192# All rights reserved.\n     3\u2192#\n     4\u2192# This source code is licensed under the BSD-style license found in the\n     5\u2192# LICENSE file in the root directory of this source tree.\n     6\u2192\n     7\u2192from pathlib import Path\n     8\u2192from typing import Any, Dict, List, Literal, Mapping, Optional, Union\n     9\u2192\n    10\u2192from torchtune.data._utils import format_content_with_images, load_image\n    11\u2192\n    12\u2192from torchtune.modules.transforms import Transform\n    13\u2192\n    14\u2192Role = Literal[\n    15\u2192    \"system\",  # Origin is system prompt\n    16\u2192    \"user\",  # Origin is user\n    17\u2192    \"assistant\",  # Origin is the model output\n    18\u2192    \"ipython\",  # Origin is return from a tool call\n    19\u2192]\n    20\u2192\n    21\u2192\n    22\u2192class Message:\n    23\u2192    \"\"\"\n    24\u2192    This class represents individual messages in a fine-tuning dataset. It supports\n    25\u2192    text-only content, text with interleaved images, and tool calls. The :class:`~torchtune.modules.tokenizers.ModelTokenizer`\n    26\u2192    will tokenize the content of the message using ``tokenize_messages`` and attach\n    27\u2192    the appropriate special tokens based on the flags set in this class.\n    28\u2192\n    29\u2192    Args:\n    30\u2192        role (Role): role of the message writer. Can be \"system\" for system prompts,\n    31\u2192            \"user\" for human prompts, \"assistant\" for model responses, or \"ipython\"\n    32\u2192            for tool call returns.\n    33\u2192        content (Union[str, List[Dict[str, Any]]]): content of the message. If it is text only content,\n    34\u2192            you can pass in a string. If it is multimodal content, pass in a list of dictionaries formatted\n    35\u2192            as follows::\n    36\u2192\n    37\u2192